# Cuboid Colony (1/1 flash, flying, trample; {G}{U}) is cast with flash at the end of Bot2's turn 2, with Bot1's Moxen untapped. Increment
# (CR 702.191a) puts a +1/+1 counter on it when Bot1 casts a spell for more mana than its power or its toughness:
#  - turn 3: A Good Day to Die ({B}, 1 mana) is not more than 1/1, so no trigger; it makes the Colony 3/1, and Capital Guard (2 mana) is more than
#    its toughness 1 (though not its power 3): a counter, 4/2 until end of turn. The ability resolves before the Guard does.
#  - turn 4: Bot2 casts a 3-mana Harrier Naga: increment is "whenever you cast", so nothing.
#  - turn 5: Cylian Elf (2 mana) is not more than the 2/2 Colony's power or toughness: no counter, equal is not greater.
# The Moxen cost nothing, so casting them triggers nothing either.

